.TH "NAVIGATOR.MAXTOUCHPOINTS" "3JS" "April 8, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Navigator.maxTouchPoints \- Navigator: maxTouchPoints property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]maxTouchPoints\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]Navigator\f[R] interface returns the maximum number of
simultaneous touch contact points that are supported by the current
device.
.SH VALUE
A number.
.PP
This value is hardware\-dependent.
Desktop computers without a touchscreen (Mac, Windows and Linux) return
0 while smartphones (Android and iOS) typically return 5.
.SH EXAMPLE
.IP
.EX
\f[B]if\f[R] (navigator.maxTouchPoints > 1) {
  \f[I]// Device supports tracking at least 2 touch points; offer complex\f[R]
  \f[I]// interaction gestures such as swiping with two/three fingers\f[R]
} \f[B]else\f[R] {
  \f[I]// Device only has 1 touch point or is not a touch screen.\f[R]
  \f[I]// Offer basic gestures such as dragging and clicking\f[R]
}
.EE
